comments.body:
nit: `forged_headers` counts the number of headers deviating from the honest chain up to that point (i.e. that batch and previous ones), whereas `accept_forged_headers` counts the additional number of headers accepted as the result of that batch. Took me a minute, and i think this could be clarified in the comment:

```suggestion
                /** The forged headers received so far, up to and including this batch. */
                const int64_t forged_headers = (batch + 1) * HEADER_BATCH_COUNT - honest;
                /** The number of forged headers that would be accepted as a result of this batch,
                 *  if the commitments in this batch and all earlier batches verify correctly. */
                const double accept_forged_headers = std::clamp<double>(forged_headers - bufsize, 0.0, HEADER_BATCH_COUNT);
```
